{"name":"Pressing My Luck","hex":"#00cc11","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pressing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Needing urgent attention.","Insistent, earnest, or persistent."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of pressure by a press or other means.","A metal or plastic part made with a press."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pressing"},{"term":"luck","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that happens to someone by chance, a chance occurrence.","A favourable chance occurrence."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To find something through good fortune; used with into, on, onto or upon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/luck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Luck","blocks":[{"text":"Luck is a phenomenon or belief that humans may associate with experiencing improbable events, especially improbably positive or negative events.\nPhilosophical naturalism, eschewing any supernatural explanations, might suggest that positive or negative events may happen at any time, and that even improbable events can happen by random chance.\nIn this view, the epithet \"lucky\" or \"unlucky\" is a descriptive label that refers to an event's positivity, negativity, or improbability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Four-leaf_clover.jpg/330px-Four-leaf_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luck"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg/250px-1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg/250px-1926WhyBeUnlucky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip